- call the complete callback for files that fail, as zmodem.h
  documents; at the moment it is only called on success.
- improve error reporting: zmodem_last_result() only says whether a
  session failed, not why.  Failures should be error codes, not log
  messages.
- make the library reentrant and threadsafe: it still keeps state in
  static variables, uses alarm()/SIGALRM for timeouts (which cancels an
  alarm set by the calling program), and only talks to stdin/stdout.
- make the log level selectable by the caller; it is fixed at "error",
  so there is no verbose output any more.
- remove the vestigial lrzsz code and options that the API cannot
  reach (TCP mode, pipe output, most file management options, ...), or
  expose them through the flags argument.
- revive the tests: "make check" runs nothing, and check.lrzsz and the
  dejagnu suite still expect the lrz and lsz programs.  Only
  "make fastcheck" works.
- look into VMIN code: how to determine if it's usable (it isn't unter
  FreeBSD and NetBSD (might have changed) and possibly many other 
  system), and what is the max value?
  Anyway - we don't *need* it. It just reduces system load (but that's
  not a real problem - zmodem over a ISDN/modem link is not much load).
- provide a way to not use any CRC check (for those people who
  a) think that lrzsz is to slow for their serial lines, or b) think
  that their transmission lines are safe. Oh well, some people don't
  learn without having pain).
